---
source: crates/sluice-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: "help(&[\"id\", \"--help\"])"
---
Print the endpoint id of this machine's identity, or replace the identity

Usage: sluice id [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON, one object per line, instead of text. A failure is then a JSON line on stderr

      --rotate
          Replace the identity with a new one, after asking

      --color <WHEN>
          When to colour help, errors and other output. NO_COLOR set to anything turns it off

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal
          - always: Colour always, unless `NO_COLOR` is set
          - never:  Never colour
          
          [default: auto]

      --yes
          Do not ask before rotating

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
